---
description: Nuxt frontend implementation conventions
globs: frontend/**/*
alwaysApply: false
---

- Use the standard Nuxt application structure and keep pages focused on presentation and interaction.
- Do not place technical-debt lifecycle decisions in Vue or Nuxt code, and do not create a Nuxt-side shadow backend.
- Keep mock data isolated so it can later be replaced by the FastAPI `/api/v1` client.
- Do not add UI/CSS frameworks, state-management libraries, or other dependencies unless the current work package requires them.
- Keep components small and explicitly named.
- Preserve governance-first, AI-second product language.
